@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ Respond to the user in **Traditional Taiwanese Chinese (繁體中文 / 台灣用
 - **Let CI start early**: push as soon as the only work left is read-only (review, reading code, writing the PR body, analysis) and run local verification **in parallel**. A CI round is 20–30 min and local verification is minutes; serialising them wastes a whole round for nothing, and a local failure means re-pushing anyway. The only gates that belong *before* a push are the second-scale ones — `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `ty check` — because they save a guaranteed-red round. Pushing a branch does **not** schedule CI (`ci.yml` triggers on `push: master` and `pull_request`); open a PR, draft is enough.
 - **Review and CI answer different questions, so run both — and believe the review.** CI only runs the tests that already exist, and defects live in the code nobody wrote a test for. A green CI is a floor, not a verdict; an adversarial review round is the verdict. Never sit idle on CI when a review could be running.
 - **A review finding cancels the CI run in flight.** That run is grading a state you are about to replace, so `gh run cancel` it, fix, commit, push, and let CI start again on the real thing. Then decide whether the fix itself needs another round: one that **replaces a mechanism** is new code and does; a comment or a one-line fix with a test pinning it does not. When a review comes back clean, let CI finish and report on it.
+- **The review budget is three rounds, and what keeps a round from finding anything is how the fix was BUILT, not how many reviews ran (#805).** Every fix starts with a test that reddens on the unfixed code and walks the path the claim names — a test that asserts after the `TestClient` exit is satisfied by the shutdown writeback and reddens on nothing. "A reads the file the way B does" is a **parity test** with B as the oracle, never two implementations kept alike by hand (three of eight inputs diverged the moment one was written). A guard that exists is not a guard that is applied: pin the line that applies it, and prove the pin by **mutating that line** (file copy, restore) and watching exactly that test redden — a mutation that reddens nothing found a test that guards nothing. Every sentence a person will read — tool reply, panel copy, docstring, plan, PR body — is written **after** the check it describes, with the evidence beside it, and every count is **derived by counting**, never recalled: the three false sentences #805's last round caught were all written the other way. Before a push, run the three lenses (conformance / veracity / regression) on your own diff; the rule above decides whether their findings buy another round.
 
